{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "TIT",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God's elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is according to godliness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before the world began;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed to me according to the commandment of God our Savior;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To Titus, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " peace, from God the Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ our Savior.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this cause I left thee in Crete, that thou shouldst set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any is blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children, not accused of riot, or disorderly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not self-willed, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For there are many disorderly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for the sake of sordid gain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One of themselves, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " always liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This testimony is true: wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men that turn from the truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the pure all things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure: but to them that are defiled and unbelieving ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They profess that they know God; but in works they deny ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", being abominable, and disobedient, and to every good work reprobate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
